      <memberdef kind="function" id="classthemis_1_1process_1_1_process_agentic_rag_1a47cbce1be690fd7567c01f58b360af2e" prot="public" static="yes" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type><ref refid="structthemis_1_1process_1_1_process_rag_context" kindref="compound">ProcessRagContext</ref></type>
        <definition>ProcessRagContext themis::process::ProcessAgenticRag::mergeDocuments</definition>
        <argsstring>(ProcessRagContext ctx, const std::vector&lt; rag::judge::RetrievedDocument &gt; &amp;extra_docs)</argsstring>
        <name>mergeDocuments</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::process::ProcessAgenticRag::mergeDocuments</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="structthemis_1_1process_1_1_process_rag_context" kindref="compound">ProcessRagContext</ref></type>
          <declname>ctx</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const std::vector&lt; rag::judge::RetrievedDocument &gt; &amp;</type>
          <declname>extra_docs</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>------------------------------------------------------------------------<mdash/> mergeDocuments – incorporate extra docs back into context ------------------------------------------------------------------------<mdash/> </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Merge additional documents back into a <ref refid="structthemis_1_1process_1_1_process_rag_context" kindref="compound">ProcessRagContext</ref>.</para>
<para>Intelligently incorporates RetrievedDocument objects back into the context, avoiding duplicates and preserving structured fields.</para>
<para>Implementation note: Uses O(n) set-based deduplication:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Builds an unordered_set of existing IDs: O(n)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>For each new document, O(1) set lookup to check if duplicate</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Overall complexity: O(n + m) where n = existing docs, m = new docs</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para>The metadata map lookup uses std::map::find() which is O(log k) where k is the size of metadata per document (typically 4-6 fields).</para>
<para>Safety: Uses RAII containers (vector, set, map) — no manual memory management.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">ctx</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Input parameter. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">extra_docs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Input parameter. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Return value. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
